# Normalise line endings on commit, check out with LF everywhere.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The differential harness compares engine output against
# reference output and the corpus format is line-oriented, so CRLF creeping into
# a trace file on a Windows contributor's machine would produce a spurious
# mismatch on Linux CI -- or, worse, a corpus that parses differently per platform.
# One canonical form in the repository is the only way to keep verdicts comparable
# across contributors and runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts, or they fail to run.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary assets are never text-normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
